* THE SYSTEM, one subcircuit: the rack, the module and the instrument, as netlisted, joined
* by the umbilical (cable.lib, instantiated by each deck between the m and i ports). Every
* part value is a BOM row or reference filled from the netlists sims.yaml names; every model
* parameter is filled from sims.yaml or of the sims it imports (params_from). What is
* behavioural, and what is left out, is in this directory's README.
*
* NODES. Node 0 is the rack PSU's ground at the far end of the bus: the receiving
* modules' ground, so every jack is read against node 0. Inside: star (BUS_GND, the
* module's header ground), agnd (AGND_MOD on module-main), agj (AGND_MOD on the jack
* board), dgnd (DIG_GND at NT-DIG-MOD), dge (DIG_GND at the etherCON, pin 8), pge
* (PWR_GND at the etherCON, pin 6), pgi (PWR_GND at U-ISO's 0V), ig (the instrument's
* PWR_GND plane at J-UMB), ag / sg (AGND_INST at the reference and at the sensor's pin 3).
*
* PORTS. m1-m8: J-UMB-MOD, the module's etherCON. i1-i8: J-UMB, the instrument's. The
* rest are the deck's controls, each a voltage against node 0: ledctl (the LED row's PWM,
* 0 blank to 1 lit), sclkctl / mosictl / csctl (the ESP32's pads, 0/1), dsck / ddin /
* dsync (U-LVL-MOD's three outputs to the DAC, 0/1), dacp (the DAC's pitch channel, volts),
* dacm1-dacm4 (the mod channels', volts), plug (every umbilical contact but +12 V, 0/1),
* pplug (the +12 V contact, 0/1), hold (the start-up scaffold, 1 holding, below).
.subckt SYS m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7 m8 i1 i2 i3 i4 i5 i6 i7 i8
+ ledctl sclkctl mosictl csctl dsck ddin dsync dacp dacm1 dacm2 dacm3 dacm4 plug pplug hold
*
* ============================ THE START-UP SCAFFOLD ============================
* TI's macromodels draw their quiescent current whatever their supply, so a cold start
* through D1/D3 or Q-INRUSH drives an unpowered rail negative and stalls the solver, and
* no DC operating point of this deck is found (README). So while `hold` is 1, ideal sources
* ramp the op-amps' rails (MODULE_ANALOG_POS12 / NEG12 on AGND_MOD, INST_POS12 on the
* instrument's plane) to near their running values through switches of r_hold - soft, so
* that once the real supply network behind them is up they carry almost nothing and
* opening them is a small step. `hold` falls long before anything is measured, and from
* then on the rails are the network's alone. Not a part.
VHP hp agnd PWL(0 0 {{t_hold_ramp}} {{ic_p12}})
SHP p12 hp hold 0 SHOLD
VHN hn agnd PWL(0 0 {{t_hold_ramp}} {{ic_n12}})
SHN n12 hn hold 0 SHOLD
VHI hi ig PWL(0 0 {{t_hold_ramp}} {{ic_ins_hold}})
SHI ins hi hold 0 SHOLD
*
* ================================ THE RACK ================================
* the PSU (its output resistance r_psu), the bus to this module's tap with the other
* modules' decoupling there, the power ribbon to the header; the bus ground from the tap
* to the PSU end, where the receivers are (node 0)
VPSUP psp 0 PWL(0 0 {{t_hold_ramp}} {{v_rail}})
RPSUP psp rpp {{r_psu}}
RBUSP rpp tapp {{r_bus_rail}}
VPSUN psn 0 PWL(0 0 {{t_hold_ramp}} {{v_rail_neg}})
RPSUN psn rpn {{r_psu}}
RBUSN rpn tapn {{r_bus_rail}}
RBUSG tapg 0 {{r_bus_seg}}
CRP tapp crp1 {{c_rack}}
RCRP crp1 crp2 {{esr_rack}}
LCRP crp2 tapg {{l_esl_rack}}
CRN tapn crn1 {{c_rack}}
RCRN crn1 crn2 {{esr_rack}}
LCRN crn2 tapg {{l_esl_rack}}
RRIBP tapp ribp {{r_rib_rail}}
LRIBP ribp bpos {{l_rib}}
RRIBN tapn ribn {{r_rib_rail}}
LRIBN ribn bneg {{l_rib}}
RRIBG star ribg {{r_rib_gnd}}
LRIBG ribg tapg {{l_rib}}
*
* ============================ MODULE POWER ENTRY ============================
* +12 V analog: PTC-POS12, D1, FB1, C1 to AGND_MOD, C-LOGIC-IN to DIG_GND. FB1 and FB3 are
* their DC resistance and C1 / C3 have no ESL here (2.2 uH is 28 mohm at 2 kHz, beside D1's
* ~3 ohm): an inductor in an op-amp's supply stalls TI's models at a cold start, whose
* quiescent currents are constant whatever the supply (README)
RPTCP bpos d1a {{r_ptc_rail}}
D1 d1a fb1a D5817
RFB1 fb1a p12 {{r_fb_dcr}}
C1 p12 c1a {{C1}}
RC1 c1a agnd {{esr_c1}}
CLGI p12 dgnd {{C-LOGIC-IN}}
* -12 V analog: PTC-NEG12, D3 (cathode at the bus), FB3, C3 to AGND_MOD
RPTCN bneg d3k {{r_ptc_rail}}
D3 fb3a d3k D5817
RFB3 n12 fb3a {{r_fb_dcr}}
C3 n12 c3a {{C3}}
RC3 c3a agnd {{esr_c3}}
* the module's own analog draw not otherwise modelled (module-own-draw): the -12 V share
* rail to rail, the rest of the +12 V share (the logic regulator's) into DIG_GND, each as a
* resistance at the rails' nominal (a constant current would drive a cold rail negative)
ROWNR p12 n12 {{r_own_rr}}
ROWNL p12 dgnd {{r_own_logic}}
* LOGIC_5V: U-REG-LOGIC, behavioural (a 5 V source on DIG_GND, on smoothly once +12 V is up:
* a kink in a source's law stalls the solver)
BLOG l5 dgnd V = {{v5}} * 0.5 * (1 + tanh((V(p12, dgnd) - {{v_logic_on}}) / 0.3))
CLGO l5 dgnd {{C-LOGIC-OUT}}
* DAC_AVDD: U-REG-DAC, the LT3042 (power-entry/sim's lt3042.lib), R-SET-DAC, C-SET-DAC
CRGI p12 agnd {{C-REG-IN}}
XREG p12 avdd setd agnd LT3042B
RSETD setd agnd {{R-SET-DAC}}
CSETD setd agnd {{C-SET-DAC}}
CRGO avdd agnd {{C-REG-OUT}}
RDACL avdd agnd {{r_dac_load}}
* U-ISO's input: PTC-ISO, D2, FB2, L-ISO-IN, L-CM-ISO on +12 V; D4 (cathode at the bus), FB4,
* L-CM-ISO on -12 V; C2 and C-ISO-IN across its pins; C-ISO-Y to PWR_GND
RPTCI bpos d2a {{r_ptc_iso}}
D2 d2a fb2a D5817
LFB2 fb2a fb2b {{l_fb_iso}}
RFB2P fb2a fb2b {{r_fb_peak}}
RFB2 fb2b liso {{r_fb_dcr}}
LISO liso lisb {{L-ISO-IN}}
RLISO lisb fp {{r_liso}}
LCA fp cma {{L-CM-ISO}}
RCA cma vinp {{r_cm_dcr}}
LCB fn cmb {{L-CM-ISO}}
RCB cmb vinn {{r_cm_dcr}}
KCM LCA LCB {{k_cm}}
RCOREA fp vinp {{r_cm_core}}
RCOREB fn vinn {{r_cm_core}}
LFB4 fn fb4b {{l_fb_iso}}
RFB4P fn fb4b {{r_fb_peak}}
RFB4 fb4b d4a {{r_fb_dcr}}
D4 d4a bneg D5817
C2 vinp c2a {{C2}}
RC2 c2a c2b {{esr_c2}}
LC2 c2b vinn {{l_esl_el}}
CISOIN vinp cin1 {{C-ISO-IN}}
LCIN cin1 vinn {{l_esl_cer}}
CY vinp cya {{C-ISO-Y}}
LCY cya pgi {{l_esl_cer}}
CISOB vinn pgi {{c_iso}}
* U-ISO, BEHAVIOURAL: its output a source at its set point behind its load regulation (r_bus),
* clamped at its lowest over-current threshold (i_ocp), then its transient response as a
* dynamic impedance (r_dyn parallel l_dyn); its input draws the output's power over its
* efficiency, instantly - no loop delay, the most of every output current step that can
* reach the rack
VSETI seti pgi PWL(0 0 {{t_hold_ramp}} {{v_bus}})
BISO pgi isx I = min({{i_ocp}}, max(0, (V(seti, pgi) - V(isx, pgi)) / {{r_bus}}))
RDYN isx isd {{r_dyn}}
LDYN isx isd {{l_dyn}}
RSNS isd isop {{r_sns}}
BIIN vinp vinn I = V(isop, pgi) * (V(isd, isop) / {{r_sns}}) / ({{eta}} * max(V(vinp, vinn), {{v_iso_in_min}}))
CISOO isop cio1 {{C-ISO-OUT}}
RCISOO cio1 pgi {{esr_iso}}
* the umbilical load switch (umbilical-load-switch/sim's behavioural LT1641), running
CDLS isop pgi {{C-DECOUPLE-LOADSW}}
RILIM isop sense {{R-ILIM}}
XU isop sense gdrv fb timer on pwrgd pgi LT1641B vlo={{vlo}} vhi={{vhi}} igate={{igate}} dvg={{dvg}} gm={{gm}} itup={{itup}} itdn={{itdn}}
RGS gdrv gnode {{R-GATE-SER}}
RGC gdrv gcm {{R-GATE-COMP}}
CGATE gcm pgi {{C-GATE-LOADSW}}
CTIMER timer pgi {{C-TIMER-LOADSW}}
M1 sense gnode umbp umbp QPASS
CISS gnode umbp {{c_iss}}
RFBH umbp fb {{R-FB-HI}}
RFBL fb pgi {{R-FB-LO}}
* the panel LED on UMBILICAL_POS12, returning to AGND_MOD on module-main (panel-led/sim's diode)
RLEDP umbp lp1 {{R-LED-PANEL}}
VVFP lp1 lp2 {{vf_shift}}
DLEDP lp2 agnd DLTL
* THE GROUNDS (dig-gnd-topology): PWR_GND on layer 4 from U-ISO to the etherCON's pin 6;
* NT-UMB-MOD to DIG_GND at pin 8; the DIG_GND plane to NT-DIG-MOD at the star; NT-AGND-MOD
* from the star to AGND_MOD; J-B2B-MOD's ground pins to the jack board
RPG4 pgi pge {{r_tie}}
RNTU pge dge {{r_tie}}
RDGP dge dgp {{r_tie}}
LDGP dgp dgnd {{l_trace}}
RNTD dgnd ntd {{r_tie}}
LNTD ntd star {{l_trace}}
RNTA star nta {{r_tie}}
LNTA nta agnd {{l_trace}}
RB2B agnd agj {{r_b2b}}
* the patch cables' sleeves: each jack's sleeve to its receiver's ground at node 0
RSLV agj 0 {{r_sleeve_eff}}
*
* ============================ MODULE: THE UMBILICAL'S NODES ============================
RPIN6 m6 pge {{r_contact}}
RPIN8 m8 dge {{r_contact}}
RPIN3 m3 umbp {{r_contact}}
* the SPI receiver (digital-and-supervision): each line's pull at the cable node, its RC and
* U-RX-MOD's input
CMS m4 dge {{c_mod}}
RPS m4 dge {{R-PULL-SCLK}}
RRS m4 srxi {{R-RX-SCLK}}
CFS srxi dge {{C-RX-SCLK}}
CRS srxi dge {{c_rx}}
CMM m5 dge {{c_mod}}
RPM m5 dge {{R-PULL-MOSI}}
RRM m5 mrxi {{R-RX-MOSI}}
CFM mrxi dge {{C-RX-MOSI}}
CRM mrxi dge {{c_rx}}
CMC m7 dge {{c_mod}}
RPC m7 l5 {{R-PULL-CS}}
RRC m7 crxi {{R-RX-CS}}
CFC crxi dge {{C-RX-CS}}
CRC crxi dge {{c_rx}}
* U-LVL-MOD's outputs to the DAC (on DAC_AVDD and DIG_GND), each a pair of switched
* resistances, through its trace into the DAC's pin capacitance on AGND_MOD; the DAC-side
* pulls (R-PULL-SCLK-DAC and R-PULL-DIN to DIG_GND, R-PULL-SYNC to DAC_AVDD)
BHS avdd osk I = V(dsck) * (V(avdd) - V(osk)) / {{r_on_lvl}}
BLS osk dgnd I = (1 - V(dsck)) * (V(osk) - V(dgnd)) / {{r_on_lvl}}
RTS osk psk {{r_trace_dac}}
CPS psk agnd {{c_dac_pin}}
RPSD psk dgnd {{R-PULL-SCLK-DAC}}
BHD avdd odi I = V(ddin) * (V(avdd) - V(odi)) / {{r_on_lvl}}
BLD odi dgnd I = (1 - V(ddin)) * (V(odi) - V(dgnd)) / {{r_on_lvl}}
RTD odi pdi {{r_trace_dac}}
CPD pdi agnd {{c_dac_pin}}
RPDD pdi dgnd {{R-PULL-DIN}}
BHY avdd osy I = V(dsync) * (V(avdd) - V(osy)) / {{r_on_lvl}}
BLY osy dgnd I = (1 - V(dsync)) * (V(osy) - V(dgnd)) / {{r_on_lvl}}
RTY osy psy {{r_trace_dac}}
CPY psy agnd {{c_dac_pin}}
RPSY psy avdd {{R-PULL-SYNC}}
*
* ======================== MODULE: BREATH RECEIVE, SHAPER, OUTPUT ========================
* breath-receive-stage: R3 from BREATH, R2 from AGND_SENSE, the bias pair, C_cm, C_diff,
* D-CLAMP-IN+/- (BAV99, as the shaper's diode fit), the INA828 (TI) and its REF from
* TRIM-BREATH-ZERO's wiper through U-REF-BUF (TI's OPA2197), the wiper at v_zero
RR3 m1 inneg {{R3}}
RR2 m2 inpos {{R2}}
RR4 inpos agnd {{R4}}
RR5 inneg agnd {{R5}}
CCMP inpos agnd {{C-CM-IN+}}
CCMN inneg agnd {{C-CM-IN-}}
CDIF inpos inneg {{C-DIFF-BREATH}}
DCL1 m2 p12 DCLAMP
DCL2 n12 m2 DCLAMP
DCL3 m1 p12 DCLAMP
DCL4 n12 m1 DCLAMP
XINA inpos inneg p12 n12 inaout refdrv rg1 rg2 INA828
RGIN rg1 rg2 {{R-GAIN-INAMP}}
RZT avdd ztop {{R-ZERO-TOP}}
RTZCW ztop zw {{r_tz_cw}}
RTZCCW zw agnd {{r_tz_ccw}}
XRFB zw refdrv p12 n12 refdrv OPAx197
* breath-response-shaper (chain.cir's, on AGND_MOD), TRIM-RESP at r_trim
RDH inaout vhalf {{R-RESP-DIV-HI}}
RDL vhalf agnd {{R-RESP-DIV-LO}}
RRIN inaout vg {{R-RESP-IN}}
RRFB vg vsh {{R-RESP-FB}}
XSA agnd vg p12 n12 vsh OPAx197
RPCW vhalf wip {{r_pot_cw}}
RPCCW wip vsh {{r_pot_ccw}}
RRESP wip tr {{R-RESP}}
RTRIM tr db {{r_trim}}
DRA vg db DRESP
DRB db vg DRESP
RRI vsh rs {{R-RESTORE-IN}}
RRF rs shaped {{R-RESTORE-FB}}
XSB agnd rs p12 n12 shaped OPAx197
* breath-output-stage: POT-GAIN, R-GAIN-FLOOR, the buffer, the summer with POT-OFFSET
* (AGND_MOD at CW, DAC_AVDD at CCW) and R-BREATH-OFFNEG from -12 V, R-OUT-PROT, and on
* the jack board C-OUT-BREATH; the jack into a receiver (r_load) at node 0
RGCW shaped gw {{r_gain_cw}}
RGCCW gw gf {{r_gain_ccw}}
RFLOOR gf agnd {{R-GAIN-FLOOR}}
XBA gw bufo p12 n12 bufo OPAx197
RBIN bufo bsum {{R-BREATH-IN}}
ROCW agnd ow {{r_off_cw}}
ROCCW ow avdd {{r_off_ccw}}
ROFF ow bsum {{R-BREATH-OFF}}
ROFFN n12 bsum {{R-BREATH-OFFNEG}}
RBFB bsum bout {{R-BREATH-FB}}
XBB agnd bsum p12 n12 bout OPAx197
RBOUT bout jb {{R-OUT-PROT}}
CBOUT jb agj {{C-OUT-BREATH}}
RBLD jb 0 {{r_load}}
*
* ============================ MODULE: THE DAC'S STAGES ============================
* the DAC8568 as code-driven ideal sources on AGND_MOD (its pins' own glitch and
* feedthrough, 0.1 nV-s, are not modelled); VREFOUT ideal at v_refout
VVRO vro agnd PWL(0 0 {{t_sig0}} 0 {{t_sig1}} {{v_refout}})
* pitch-stage (pitch-stage.lib's PSTAGE, on AGND_MOD), TRIM-GAIN and TRIM-OFFSET where
* t_gain and w_offset put them; C-FILT-PITCH and D-ESD-PITCH on the jack board
BDP dpin agnd V = V(dacp)
RBDP dpin agnd {{R-BIAS-DAC}}
RTOCW vro wipo {{r_toff_cw}}
RTOCCW wipo agnd {{r_toff_ccw}}
RINJ wipo vsum {{R-VREF-INJ}}
RVSER vro vsum {{R-VREF-SER}}
XRBP vsum vfb p12 n12 vrefb OPAx197
RVFB vrefb vfb {{R-VREF-FB}}
RVGND vfb agnd {{R-VREF-GND}}
RCTR vrefb r1b {{R-GAIN-CTR}}
RN1 r1b pminus {{RN-PITCH}}
RN2 pminus gtm {{RN-PITCH}}
RTG gtm jp {{r_trim_gain}}
RINP dpin pplus {{R-OPAMP-IN}}
CAAP pplus agnd {{C-AA-PITCH}}
XPA pplus pminus p12 n12 pout OPAx197
CFBP pout pminus {{C-FB-PITCH}}
ROUTP pout jp {{R-OUT-PROT}}
CFLP jp agj {{C-FILT-PITCH}}
CESDP jp agj {{c_esd}}
RVCOP jp 0 {{r_vco}}
* mod-channels: DAC ch7 through R-OPAMP-IN-REF into the reference follower; each channel
* x(1 + R-MODGAIN-FB/R-MODGAIN-IN) against it, R-OUT-PROT, C-FILT-MOD on the jack board
VD7 d7 agnd PWL(0 0 {{t_sig0}} 0 {{t_sig1}} {{v_ref7}})
RBD7 d7 agnd {{R-BIAS-DAC-CH7}}
RID7 d7 refp {{R-OPAMP-IN-REF}}
XREFM refp vrefm p12 n12 vrefm OPAx197
BDM1 dm1 agnd V = V(dacm1)
RBM1 dm1 agnd {{R-BIAS-DAC-1}}
RIM1 dm1 pm1 {{R-OPAMP-IN-1}}
R1M1 vrefm mm1 {{R1-1}}
R2M1 mm1 om1 {{R2-1}}
XM1 pm1 mm1 p12 n12 om1 OPAx197
ROM1 om1 jm1 {{R-OUT-PROT-1}}
CFM1 jm1 agj {{C-FILT-MOD-1}}
RLM1 jm1 0 {{r_vco}}
BDM2 dm2 agnd V = V(dacm2)
RBM2 dm2 agnd {{R-BIAS-DAC-2}}
RIM2 dm2 pm2 {{R-OPAMP-IN-2}}
R1M2 vrefm mm2 {{R1-2}}
R2M2 mm2 om2 {{R2-2}}
XM2 pm2 mm2 p12 n12 om2 OPAx197
ROM2 om2 jm2 {{R-OUT-PROT-2}}
CFM2 jm2 agj {{C-FILT-MOD-2}}
RLM2 jm2 0 {{r_vco}}
BDM3 dm3 agnd V = V(dacm3)
